  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) van&#39;t Hoff factor, it is used in measuring colligative properties</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>&#160;Normal molar mass&#160;</mtext><mtext>&#160;Abnormal molar mass&#160;</mtext></mfrac></math></p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math> Cryoscopic constant or molal freezing constant</p><p>(C) Solutions with same osmotic pressure are known as isotonic solutions.</p><p>(D) Solutions with same composition of vapour over them are called Azeotrope or azeotrophic mixtures.</p>"
